**[To_Make_a_migration]**
*1.Generate the file*
npx prisma migrate dev --name example_name --create-only
*2.this will create the example sql code without running into the db, you edit this sql file and to run it to db:* 
npx prisma migrate dev


**[Table_Relationships__1-M]**
model User {
  id  String @id @default(uuid())
  tokens Token[] // [1].The User has many tokens
}
model Token{
  userId String // [2].The Foriegn key
  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id]) // [3]. The Connection 
}

*After Changing the prisma schema, you must restart the prisma client;*
npx prisma generate

If a migration file is recoreded in postgres' _prisma_migrations table but the sql itself isn't applied to the db
Delete the migration file from that table and run the migration again


[22/4]🌟🌟🌟If You added a column that should be requied, but sql says there's rows where its null and preventing the migration
1- Add the column and let it be null
2- Alter table and give all the rows a defualt value (isActive:true)
3- Alter the table again & alter the column and make it NOT NULL

